# Archived regulatory sources are evidence, not text files. A rule records the
# sha256 of the document it was drafted against, so these bytes must be
# identical in every checkout on every platform. Without this, git translates
# line endings on a Windows checkout and the recorded hash stops matching —
# which is precisely how it happened once: the hashes in V0012 were the CRLF
# working-copy hashes and CI, checking out LF, read three mismatches.
db/sources/** -text
db/tests/fixtures/** -text
